{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nst=json.load(open('../state.json'))\ncur=[i for i in st['interpretations'] if i.get('id')=='563c3a9abeea4d1aa35cd5e8a3b0497c-interpretation-0'][0]\nV2=\\\"f5bf67e282cb41c185854215b5b28e34\\\"\nlim=[l for l in cur['limitations'] if not l.startswith('The change was triggered through AddVoter')]\nlim.insert(0,\\\"The command-coverage revision measured all three triggers with the dual-interface FSM and the control, but its declared comparisons were unresolved because the setup event did not carry the trigger field, so those values are cited from the result events rather than from satisfied comparisons; a corrected revision is submitted with this update.\\\")\nlim.append(\\\"The change was triggered through AddVoter with a new address, AddNonvoter and RemoveServer; DemoteVoter and the deprecated Promote command were not measured.\\\")\ninterp={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"1995fd2023c948c99b650dce1b597cd6-question-0\\\",\n \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"0c2ccd3e54bd41d385d13c33edaec69f-experiment\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":list(dict.fromkeys(cur['source_ids']+[\\\"next_configuration_commands\\\"])),\n \\\"executions\\\":{**cur['executions'], V2:[0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7]},\n \\\"conclusion\\\":cur['conclusion'],\\\"defect_claim\\\":cur['defect_claim'],\n \\\"rationale\\\":(cur['rationale']+\\\" \\\"\n  \\\"A third execution covered other configuration commands and its result events carry the same shape (receipt f5bf67e282cb41c185854215b5b28e34, result events at parsed indices 1, 3, 5 and 7): the dual-interface FSM recorded 0 StoreConfiguration calls and 6, 6 and 5 ApplyBatch configuration entries after a voter address change, an AddNonvoter and a RemoveServer respectively, while the ConfigurationStore-only control recorded 6 and 0. Its declared comparisons came back unresolved rather than satisfied because the setup event did not carry the trigger field the identity used, so a corrected revision that adds that field to the setup event is submitted with this update; the values themselves are read from the result events, which carry the trigger and both counters. What the run adds is that the missing callback is not specific to one command: three different configuration changes produced the same zero.\\\"),\n \\\"knowledge\\\":cur['knowledge'],\\\"answers\\\":{},\\\"counterevidence\\\":cur['counterevidence'],\n \\\"limitations\\\":lim,\n \\\"joint_history\\\":cur['joint_history']}\nd={\\\"rationale\\\":(\\\"Interpreted the command-coverage receipt and fixed the harness omission it exposed. The result events show the same zero StoreConfiguration calls for all three dual-interface triggers (voter address change, AddNonvoter, RemoveServer) with 6, 6 and 5 ApplyBatch configuration entries and the control at 6 and 0, so the missing callback is not specific to one command; but the declared comparisons were unresolved because the setup event lacked the trigger field used as identity, so this update cites the result events for those values, records that limitation, and submits a corrected revision that adds the field to the setup event with the same cases and comparisons. No earlier receipt is withdrawn and no claim is weakened: the finding rests on the first two executions' satisfied comparisons plus these event values.\\\"),\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[interp],\n \\\"experiment\\\":{\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"1995fd2023c948c99b650dce1b597cd6-question-0\\\",\\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n  \\\"previous_id\\\":\\\"0c2ccd3e54bd41d385d13c33edaec69f-experiment\\\",\n  \\\"revision_reason\\\":\\\"The previous revision added two triggers but emitted the setup event without the trigger field, so the identity built from batching_fsm and trigger could not be matched and all four comparisons came back unresolved. This revision adds trigger to the setup event; cases, counters and comparisons are otherwise identical.\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"batching_fsm_iface\\\",\\\"config_store_iface\\\",\\\"fsm_single_apply\\\",\\\"fsm_batch_apply\\\",\\\"next_configuration_commands\\\"],\n  \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Four cases as in the previous revision - a ConfigurationStore-only control and three dual-interface cases triggered by a voter address change, an AddNonvoter and a RemoveServer - each reporting the StoreConfiguration and ApplyBatch configuration counts, with the setup event now carrying the same trigger identifier as the result event so the admission can be matched.\\\",\n   \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"All three commands are legal on a three-voter cluster, as before.\\\",\n    \\\"The setup and result events now share batching_fsm and trigger, which is the identity the comparisons use.\\\",\n    \\\"The recorder is still shared across the cluster's FSMs.\\\"],\n   \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"DemoteVoter and the deprecated Promote command.\\\"]},\n  \\\"prefix\\\":(\\\"Each case calls MakeClusterCustom with three peers, bootstrapping and the in-memory test configuration, and a MakeFSMFunc returning either an FSM implementing FSM and ConfigurationStore or one that also implements ApplyBatch, all recording into a shared recorder. The case emits assurance_config_store_setup with the batching flag, the trigger name, the leader and target identities and the peer count, issues exactly one configuration command according to the trigger (AddVoter with a new address for the target voter, AddNonvoter for a fresh identity, or RemoveServer of the target follower), waits up to five seconds for a callback counter to become non-zero, waits a further 200ms, and emits assurance_config_store_result with the same trigger and batching flags plus the command's error and the counts. The harness is TestAssuranceConfigurationStoreWithBatching.\\\"),\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"setup\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_config_store_setup\\\"}],\n  \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_config_store_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"batching_fsm\\\",\\\"trigger\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"setup\\\",\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"store_configuration_calls\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"ne\\\",\\\"value\\\":0},\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"batching_fsm\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"trigger\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"add-nonvoter\\\"}],\\\"description\\\":\\\"Dual-interface FSM after an AddNonvoter: whether the documented callback arrives.\\\"},\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_config_store_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"batching_fsm\\\",\\\"trigger\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"setup\\\",\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"store_configuration_calls\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"ne\\\",\\\"value\\\":0},\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"batching_fsm\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"trigger\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"remove-follower\\\"}],\\\"description\\\":\\\"Dual-interface FSM after a RemoveServer: whether the documented callback arrives.\\\"},\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_config_store_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"batching_fsm\\\",\\\"trigger\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"setup\\\",\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"store_configuration_calls\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"ne\\\",\\\"value\\\":0},\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"batching_fsm\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"trigger\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"move-voter-address\\\"}],\\\"description\\\":\\\"The standing dual-interface case, re-measured with the others.\\\"},\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_config_store_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"batching_fsm\\\",\\\"trigger\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"setup\\\",\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"store_configuration_calls\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"ne\\\",\\\"value\\\":0},\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"batching_fsm\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"trigger\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"move-voter-address\\\"}],\\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: the ConfigurationStore-only FSM receives the callback.\\\"}]}}\njson.dump(d,open('update.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False); open('update.json','a').write('\\\\n')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
