{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Interpreted the command-coverage receipt and repaired the harness omission it exposed. The result events show the same zero StoreConfiguration calls for all three dual-interface triggers — a voter address change, an AddNonvoter and a RemoveServer — with 6, 6 and 5 ApplyBatch configuration entries and the ConfigurationStore-only control at 6 and 0, so the missing callback is not specific to one command; the declared comparisons came back unresolved because the setup event did not carry the trigger field used as identity, so I cited the result events for those values, recorded that as a limitation, and submitted a corrected revision that adds the field with the same cases and comparisons. The account's earlier satisfied comparisons and receipts are unchanged and the finding is not weakened, and joint history explains how the two experiments' receipts compose. About twenty-five minutes of run time remain; the outstanding item is interpreting the corrected revision's receipt, and if the run ends before it arrives the request stands as a fixed experiment with its prediction recorded.\"}"}}
